  ('Bachelor of Accounting', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Multimedia University Malaysia (MMU)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 5764, '3 years', '["Mar","Jul","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Accounting (Hons.) at MMU University Malaysia is a three-year program that prepares students to become professional accountants, recognized by the Malaysian Institute of Accountants This degree equips graduates with the essential knowledge and skills needed to make informed financial decisions and contribute effectively to business leadership

The curriculum covers critical areas of accounting, including digital and entrepreneurial skills, ensuring that students are well-prepared for the evolving landscape of the profession The program also incorporates A’adab©, emphasizing the importance of ethical values in professional interactions and environmental stewardship, as outlined in the Halatuju 4 Program Perakaunan by the Malaysian Institute of Accountants

With a commitment to maintaining professional body exemptions despite the transition from a four-year to a three-year study duration, MMU ensures that graduates are fully equipped to qualify as Chartered Accountants Malaysia (C.A. (M)) after gaining the relevant professional experience

Overall, this program not only provides a solid foundation in accounting principles but also instills the values and ethics essential for success in the accounting profession, preparing students for a meaningful and impactful career in the field.

Pass Matriculation / Foundation or its equivalent, with minimum CGPA 2.00 including a minimum of Grade C in English at SPM/O-Level or its equivalent.', '[{"year":"Year 1","modules":["English for Business Studies","Quantitative Analysis","Microeconomics","Fundamental to Financial Accounting","Management","Introduction to Cyberpreneurship","English for Business Communication","Management Accounting i","Financial Accounting & Reporting I","Principles of Finance","Macroeconomics","Principles of Marketing"]},{"year":"Year 2","modules":["Financial Accounting andReporting II","Accounting InformationSystems I","Taxation I","Auditing","Management Accounting II","Taxation II","Corporate Finance","Organisational Behavior","Commercial Law"]},{"year":"Year 3","modules":["Professional Ethics","Corporate Accounting I","Accounting Information Systems II","Company Law and SecretarialPractice","Accounting Theory","Securities Investment andPortfolio Management","Advanced Auditing","Public Sector Accounting","Corporate Accounting II","Practical Training"]},{"year":"Year 4","modules":["Advanced Taxation","Advanced Accounting","Information SystemsAccounting","Advanced Management","Management DecisionScience Strategy","Corporate Strategy","Integrated Case Study"]}]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Professional accountants that may specialise in taxation, forensic accounting and investigation, auditing, management accounting, financial accounting, public sector accounting, accounting information systems, academician, consultant, and shared services."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Pass Matriculation / Foundation or its equivalent, with minimum CGPA 2.00 including a minimum of Grade C in English at SPM/O-Level or its equivalent.

