  ('Bachelor of Arts (Honours) in Global Sustainable Tourism', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UCSI University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 5269, '3 years', '["Jan","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Arts (Honours) in Global Sustainable Tourism at UCSI University equips graduates to drive positive change in the tourism sector by addressing critical global challenges such as climate change, cultural preservation, and social equity. By implementing sustainable practices and innovative solutions, graduates can transform tourism into a force for good, contributing to the conservation of natural resources, the empowerment of local communities, and the promotion of cross-cultural understanding.

Students can expect a dynamic and engaging learning environment that combines theoretical knowledge with practical applications. The program includes a blend of lectures, case studies, field trips, and hands-on projects that simulate real-world scenarios in the tourism industry. This immersive approach prepares students to tackle complex sustainability issues, develop critical thinking skills, and foster creativity in problem-solving.

Through collaborative work, internships, and interactions with industry experts, students gain valuable experience and build a professional network, positioning them to make a meaningful impact in the field of sustainable tourism upon graduation.

