  ('Diploma in Nursing', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UCSI University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Diploma', 4862, '3 years', '["Jan","Jul"]'::jsonb, 'The Diploma in Nursing Program at UCSI University Malaysia offers a comprehensive education in both academic and clinical aspects of nursing. It focuses on providing compassionate care to patients with various health conditions and builds a strong foundation in basic sciences and nursing theories. Graduates are equipped with the skills to treat, rehabilitate, and educate patients, families, and communities. The program is recognized by the Malaysian Nursing Board (MNB) and the Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA), with a 100% passing rate for the MNB examinations.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., TOEFL PBT, equivalent, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

This programme prepares graduates for a broad spectrum of first-level practice roles in hospital and community health centres. It fosters a commitment to lifelong learning, critical reflective thinking and professional growth. The diploma is internationally recognised and allows graduates to work in any country, subject to registration requirements.

After three (3) years of work experience, graduates will be able to further develop professionally through the Bachelor of Nursing Programme, which will enable the nurses to pursue other expanded roles and different kinds of career opportunities.

