  ('Master in Science Diplomacy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UCSI University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Diploma', 9603, '1 year', '["Jan","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master in Science Diplomacy at UCSI University positions students at the forefront of global change, bridging the gap between scientific innovation and international policy-making. As the world increasingly relies on scientific understanding to tackle global challenges, science diplomacy has emerged as a crucial tool for fostering international collaboration and policy development.

This program equips you with the skills to be a leader at the intersection of science and diplomacy, preparing you to address critical global issues such as climate change, health pandemics, and technological innovation. You will learn how to influence international policy, promote scientific cooperation, and serve as an honest broker driving transformative solutions on the global stage.

The interdisciplinary curriculum seamlessly integrates scientific knowledge with diplomatic skills, preparing students to tackle complex global challenges effectively. You will learn from expert faculty that includes leading academics and practitioners in science and international relations, providing valuable insights from both fields. Additionally, the program facilitates connections with professionals and experts worldwide, helping you build a robust global network that spans countries and disciplines.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g.,Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Science Diplomat\nInternational Policy Advisor\nEnvironmental Negotiator\nGlobal Health Strategist\nResearch Analyst in International Organization"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A bachelor’s degree in the field of Science Diplomacy or related fields with a minimum CGPA of 2.50 or equivalent, as accepted by the HEP Senate.

