  ('Master of Architecture', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UCSI University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 6036, '2 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'UCSI University''s Master of Architecture programme emphasises design, technology, sustainability, and industry involvement. Students acquire hands-on experience by working on real-world projects with developers and agencies over the course of two years. The programme includes Building Information Modelling (BIM) courses, which use modern technology to address complicated design issues. Sustainability is a top priority, providing chances for research cooperation and industrial networking. Students hone their technical skills and investigate national and global architectural issues through studio work, lectures, and seminar sessions. Overall, the programme offers a complete education as well as important networking opportunities for potential professional progression in architecture.

