  ('Master of Child Psychology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UCSI University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 6666, '1.5 years', '["Jan","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Child Psychology program at UCSI University empowers students with essential insights and expertise to thrive in the specialized realm of child psychology. Covering a comprehensive range of developmental aspects, students gain a deep understanding of how children learn and engage with their environment. The program is designed to deliver thorough training and applied knowledge, fostering an appreciation for the role of subjectivities in optimizing children''s development. Whether pursued through applied or research pathways, the program accommodates diverse learning preferences, including full-time and part-time options tailored to the demanding schedules of today''s educators. The curriculum encompasses intensive sessions on various topics, from child self-concept to attachment theories, shaping graduates into highly adaptable and forward-thinking educators. With a focus on peer-to-peer learning and collaboration among professionals from diverse fields, this Master''s program stands out as the preferred choice for educators, offering a future-proof gateway to advanced education and a smarter approach to cultivating the next generation.

A Bachelor''s Degree in Psychology or its equivalent with minimum CGPA 2.75 (Note: A Bachelor''s Degree in Psychology with minimum CGPA of 2.5 can be accepted subject to rigorous internal assessment by an independent review panel.

