  ('Master of Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UCSI University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 7335, '1 year', '["Jan","May","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Science (MSc) in Actuarial Management programme at UCSI University is a graduate-level programme that provides a complete education in actuarial sciences. It encompasses the first four CAS/SOA exams and leads to a Master''s degree. The programme has two structures to meet the needs of different learners: Structure C, which is appropriate for professionals from quantitative disciplines looking to make a career change into actuarial work, and Structure B, which is designed for individuals with prior actuarial knowledge looking to deepen their theoretical understanding and research skills. Overall, the programme strives to provide graduates with the technical expertise and managerial skills required for success in the actuarial sector and beyond.

