  ('Bachelor of Finance and Economics', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Taylor''s University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 8775, '3 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Finance and Economics (Honours) Program at Taylor''s University Malaysia  is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of economic behavior and a deep knowledge of the financial sector. It integrates modern theories in economics and finance to equip students with analytical skills and knowledge needed to navigate complex financial markets. Students will learn about capital markets, investment decision-making, option pricing, and macroeconomic factors impacting national economies. The program offers a methodological approach to analyze and evaluate financial complexities. Graduates from this program will be equipped for high-responsibility roles in the economic and financial system, including positions in financial institutions, international organizations, supervisory authorities, and central banks.

