  ('Bachelor of Food Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Taylor''s University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10761, '3 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Food Science (Hons) programme at Taylor''s University provides students with a comprehensive understanding of food processing, food texture, flavor, nutritional composition, sensory evaluation, and food safety. The programme aims to equip students with the knowledge and skills necessary for the development of nutritious and safe food products.

Throughout the programme, students will delve into various aspects of food science, including food chemistry, food microbiology, food engineering, food analysis, food quality assurance, and food product development. They will also gain practical experience through laboratory work, research projects, and industry internships, enabling them to apply their knowledge in real-world settings.

The programme is designed to be compatible with the new Taylor''s Curriculum Framework, allowing students to personalize their learning experience by mixing and matching study modules according to their interests and career goals.

Min. CGPA 2.00 for 2 subjects including (ANY 2) subjects: Biology, Physics / Mathematics, Chemistry

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["After completing the Bachelor of Food Science (Hons) programme at Taylor''s University, graduates can pursue careers as food analysts, food product specialists, food technologists, production managers, quality assurance associates, regulatory affairs officers, research scientists (food), and more.\nEducation pathway"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Sijil Tinggi Persekolahan Malaysia (STPM)

