  ('Bachelor of Mechanical Engineering with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Taylor''s University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10426, '4 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Mechanical Engineering with Honours at Taylor''s University is a comprehensive degree programme designed to provide students with a strong foundation in fundamental theories and concepts of mechanical engineering. This programme focuses on equipping students with the scientific knowledge and problem-solving skills necessary to tackle challenges and design systems in various industries such as automotive, power generation, aerospace, and manufacturing.

Throughout the programme, students will develop a deep understanding of mechanical engineering principles and gain proficiency in applying physics and mathematical concepts to real-world problems. This prepares them for a wide range of career opportunities in the digital economy.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Upon completion of the programme, graduates are well-prepared to embark on a fulfilling career journey. The Bachelor of Mechanical Engineering opens doors to a diverse array of professions, including aerospace engineering, aircraft engineering, automotive engineering, industrial engineering, and manufacturing engineering. Additionally, graduates can pursue roles as materials engineers, mechatronic and robotic engineers, medical engineers, product development engineers, project engineers, and systems engineers. This wide range of career options showcases the versatility of the programme and the opportunities it offers to aspiring engineers.

This component aims to develop critical thinking, build up social intelligence and cultivate civic responsibility as well as broaden cultural knowledge. These consist of compulsory and nationally-mandated study modules required by the Malaysian Ministry of Higher Education.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Upon completion of the programme, graduates are well-prepared to embark on a fulfilling career journey. The Bachelor of Mechanical Engineering opens doors to a diverse array of professions, including aerospace engineering, aircraft engineering, automotive engineering, industrial engineering, and manufacturing engineering. Additionally, graduates can pursue roles as materials engineers, mechatronic and robotic engineers, medical engineers, product development engineers, project engineers, and systems engineers. This wide range of career options showcases the versatility of the programme and the opportunities it offers to aspiring engineers."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Sijil Tinggi Persekolahan Malaysia (STPM)

