  ('Bachelor of Mechatronics Engineering with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Taylor''s University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10426, '4 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Mechatronics Engineering with Honours at Taylor’s University Malaysia is designed to provide a strong foundation in the core principles of mechatronics, an interdisciplinary field integrating mechanical, electrical, and computer engineering

Throughout the program, students explore the design, development, and control of smart systems and devices that combine mechanical, electronic, and software components The curriculum covers a wide range of topics, including robotics, automation, sensors and actuators, embedded systems, and control engineering Students will learn to design and implement intelligent systems, utilizing cutting-edge technologies that shape industries such as manufacturing, automotive, healthcare, and aerospace

A key feature of the program is the emphasis on hands-on learning and industry engagement Students have opportunities to participate in practical projects, internships, and collaborative research, applying theoretical knowledge to real-world challenges This approach ensures graduates possess the technical expertise and problem-solving skills needed to excel in the evolving field of mechatronics

Taylor’s University welcomes applicants from around the world, with many students recognizing the exceptional quality and opportunities the program offers, making the admissions process competitive.

