  ('Bachelor of Quantity Surveying', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Taylor''s University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 7944, '3.5 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Quantity Surveying (Hons) at Taylor''s University is a professional degree programme that offers a recognized qualification in Quantity Surveying, a crucial role in the construction industry. This programme provides students with the necessary knowledge and skills to excel in the field and offers a pathway toward becoming a Registered Quantity Surveyor.

One of the key advantages of this programme is that graduates gain automatic membership to the Board of Quantity Surveyors Malaysia (BQSM). This recognition demonstrates their competency and professionalism in the field of Quantity Surveying. Additionally, the programme is accredited by the Pacific Association of Quantity Surveyors (PAQS), further enhancing graduates'' qualifications and employability.

Taylor''s University also ensures that graduates are future-proofed with broader graduate capabilities beyond academic knowledge. The programme focuses on a balanced attainment set, equipping students with practical skills, critical thinking abilities, and professional ethics.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Upon completing the Bachelor of Quantity Surveying (Hons) programme, graduates have a wide range of exciting career opportunities in the construction and civil engineering industries. Some of the potential career paths include Building Material Manager, Building Surveyor, Construction Manager, Consultant Quantity Surveyor, Contractor Quantity Surveyor, Developer Quantity Surveyor, Geomatic and Land Surveyor, Mechanical and Electrical Quantity Surveyor, and Property Management, Valuation, and Estate Agency Surveyor. These diverse career options demonstrate the versatility and breadth of expertise gained through the programme.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Upon completing the Bachelor of Quantity Surveying (Hons) programme, graduates have a wide range of exciting career opportunities in the construction and civil engineering industries. Some of the potential career paths include Building Material Manager, Building Surveyor, Construction Manager, Consultant Quantity Surveyor, Contractor Quantity Surveyor, Developer Quantity Surveyor, Geomatic and Land Surveyor, Mechanical and Electrical Quantity Surveyor, and Property Management, Valuation, and Estate Agency Surveyor. These diverse career options demonstrate the versatility and breadth of expertise gained through the programme."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Sijil Tinggi Persekolahan Malaysia (STPM)

