  ('Bachelor of Science (Honours) in Architecture', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Taylor''s University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10729, '3 years', '["Feb","Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Science (Honours) in Architecture at Taylor''s University is a pre-professional degree programme that is accredited by the Board of Architects Malaysia (Lembaga Arkitek Malaysia - LAM). This programme exempts graduates from the LAM Part I Examination, providing a streamlined path towards becoming Assistant Architects. Students also have the option to further their studies and become Graduate Architects.

Throughout the programme, students gain a comprehensive understanding of architectural design principles and develop practical skills in areas such as architectural modeling, photography, structural specialization, computer-aided design (CAD), 3D visualization, and conceptualization. The curriculum is designed to nurture creativity, critical thinking, and technical expertise, preparing students for a successful career in architecture.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Upon graduation, students can pursue a variety of exciting career paths. These include roles as architectural model specialists, architectural photographers, architectural structure specialists, computer-aided design/3D visualizers, interior designers/interior architects, resort/hotel architectural conceptualizers, theme park conceptual architects, and town planning conceptual architects. The programme offers a broad range of career opportunities, allowing graduates to specialize in their areas of interest and contribute to the built environment.

