  ('Master of Philosophy in Immersive Technologies and Video Game Studies', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'APU University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 3520, '2 years', '["May","Jun","Jul","Aug","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Master of Philosophy in Immersive Technologies and Video Game Studies — APU Malaysia

A research-focused MPhil preparing immersive experience designers and scholars. The programme develops advanced technical expertise in immersive technologies, innovation and idea management, and deep domain knowledge across management and computing. It also provides advanced research training and skills to pursue a PhD and roles such as Interactive Experience Designer, Advanced UX Strategist, Immersive Digital Innovation Specialist, or Immersive Technology Scholar–Practitioner.

The Asia Pacific University of Technology & Innovation (APU) has launched its new Game Development Lab & Studio, built to mirror professional international studios.The facility supports APU’s industry-focused game development programs and its role as Malaysia’s e-Sports Focus Centre (appointed by the Ministry of Higher Education).Equipped with high-performance workstations (RTX 5070 GPUs and Intel Core Ultra CPUs), it gives students hands-on experience with industry-standard tools.With real-world-experienced lecturers and guidance from curriculum partners like Larian Studios, graduates are prepared for careers in game development and immersive digital media.

APU has unveiled Malaysia’s first university-curated, publicly accessible Video Games Mini Museum. The collection highlights landmark moments in gaming history, featuring consoles such as the Magnavox Odyssey—the world’s first commercially released home video game system—and the iconic Atari 2600 in its various forms. Visitors can also view a complete lineup of Nintendo hardware spanning generations from 1977 to 2006, along with classic game arcade exhibits.

More than a static display, the museum demonstrates APU’s dedication to combining historical insight, industry relevance, and hands-on learning. It gives students and the public an opportunity to explore the technological, cultural, and social development of video games.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Interactive Experience Designer\nAdvanced User Experience Strategist\nImmersive Digital Innovation Specialist\nImmersive Technology Scholar - Practitioner"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Bachelor’s degree in related fields with a minimum CGPA of 2.75, or its equivalent qualification as accepted by the Senate.

