Throughout the program, students will delve into a wide array of topics, including cost accounting, financial accounting, managerial accounting, corporate accounting, accounting information systems, auditing and assurance, international financial reporting standards (IFRS), generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), stakeholder values and ethics, issues in financial reporting, information technology for accountants, quantitative methods, corporate finance, organizational behavior, business economics, business law, company and association law, taxation law and practices, financial statements, investment analysis, cost management, innovation and entrepreneurship, and advanced business communication.

