  ('Bachelor of Biomedical Sciences (Hons) - Online Degree', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3900, '4 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'This program emphasizes the functioning of cells, organs, and systems within the human body, a fascinating and dynamic field that is crucial for understanding and treating human diseases. As new strains of diseases continue to emerge, negatively impacting community health, biomedical science will play a vital role in healthcare delivery. Accurate disease diagnosis is essential, as patients'' lives heavily depend on the results of clinical laboratory investigations performed by skilled biomedical scientists. Consequently, the field of biomedical science is set to expand, particularly in Malaysia, where the healthcare system is experiencing rapid growth.

The aim of this course is to guide students in a structured manner as they orient themselves and train in areas of specific professional interest. It seeks to provide fundamental knowledge and build the skills necessary for successful career advancement, ensuring graduates are both employable and trainable. Additionally, the program focuses on developing laboratory skills, including experiment planning, data acquisition, management, and analysis related to selected research problems.

Delivery methods include asynchronous e-learning (online learning materials), synchronous e-learning (online teaching), face-to-face lectures and tutorials, as well as practical sessions at designated learning centers.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

