  ('Bachelor of Engineering (Hons) in Medical Electronics Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 0, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Engineering (Hons) in Medical Electronics Engineering at MAHSA University is a comprehensive 4-year specialist program designed for individuals passionate about engineering and eager to make a significant contribution to medical science and healthcare enhancement

This program prepares students to become medical electronics engineers, the vital professionals responsible for designing, testing, manufacturing, and maintaining the health equipment that doctors and hospitals rely on every day The curriculum offers in-depth exposure to essential subjects including engineering mathematics, engineering chemistry, engineering physics, electronics and electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, civil engineering, network analysis, logic design, analogue and digital circuits, control systems, medical physics, and more

Upon completing the program, graduates will possess a thorough understanding of the operations of advanced medical equipment They will be equipped to correctly identify and analyze problems, apply computing solutions, design and implement computer medical systems, and utilize the latest tools and techniques to enhance healthcare delivery Students will also gain insights into health and safety issues related to medical electronic systems and equipment, as well as uphold ethical and environmental standards in healthcare provision

This specialized engineering program not only equips students with technical skills but also prepares them for various expert responsibilities in the healthcare sector, making them well-positioned to impact patient care positively and advance the field of medical technology.

