  ('Bachelor of Information Technology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4112, '3 years', '["Jan","May","Aug","Jan"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Information Technology (Hons) is a three-year program developed in consultation with a panel of experts and approved by the Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA). This program offers four distinct areas of specialization: Data Management, Game Computing, Mobile Computing, and Network Computing, allowing students to select their preferred path to acquire the essential knowledge and industry-specific technological skills.

After completing seven semesters, students will undertake industrial training at the end of Year 3, Semester 2. Following this training, students must submit a report, while the industry partners are required to assess and report on the students’ job performance. This industrial training is crucial for meeting MQA accreditation requirements, providing students with real-world experience in preparing reports on technical work and projects. The program equips students with advanced theoretical and practical skills while also introducing them to strategic planning and project management.

In their final year, the research project component of the program will enable students to engage in research and development with a focus on commercialization. This aspect will help them develop both the academic and practical dimensions of their chosen field, while reinforcing independent learning skills. Through this process, students will demonstrate advanced critical thinking, analytical abilities, and problem-solving skills, all of which will enhance their employability.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

