  ('Bachelor of Science (Hons) in Islamic Finance', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 2933, '3.5 years', '["Jan","May","Aug","Jan"]'::jsonb, 'According to the World Bank, Islamic finance has emerged as an effective tool for financing development globally, including in non-Muslim countries. This sector is one of the fastest-growing segments of the financial industry in various regions, having achieved double-digit growth rates over the past decade despite global challenges. Its influence has expanded beyond traditional Islamic markets, establishing strong presences in banking, takaful (Islamic insurance), and capital markets.

