  ('Diploma in Paramedical Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Diploma', 3227, '3 years', '["Jan","May","Aug","Jan"]'::jsonb, 'Paramedics are often the first responders during critical moments, providing emergency care and potentially saving lives. They manage the emergency treatment of sick or injured individuals in out-of-hospital settings.

If you are compassionate, caring, and capable of handling stressful and dynamic situations, a career as a Paramedic can be immensely rewarding.

You will receive training in clinical decision-making, patient assessment, interpretation of life-threatening cardiac rhythms, defibrillation, drug therapy, and airway management. You will develop knowledge, skills, and attitudes that align with international professional standards.

As a paramedic, you play a vital role in the continuum of care and act as a crucial link to health resources. Your responsibilities will also include public education, health promotion, and participation in injury and illness prevention programs. Career opportunities for paramedics have expanded to include private ambulance services.

