  ('Doctor of Philosophy by Research', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 3839, '3 years', '["Jan","May","Aug","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Management is a traditional doctoral qualification encompassing a broad range of management disciplines. It provides an opportunity for in-depth research, with outcomes that contribute to the advancement of knowledge. While it includes a theoretical component, the research program also allows academicians and managers to investigate specialized areas with practical applications.

The PhD in Management at MAHSA University is particularly suitable for practicing managers, academicians, and researchers who aspire to make significant leadership contributions within their organizations or are considering a career in academia. Graduates of the program are expected to enhance knowledge in their chosen fields. The research methods employed at MAHSA are work-applied, utilizing action research, case studies, or reflective practice. This research is designed to be of practical value both to the candidate and the organization involved in the study.

Although there is no quick route to completing a PhD in Management, the program is structured to help candidates achieve their goals in the shortest timeframe compatible with high-quality research. Progress is systematic and progressive, supported by a nurturing environment that includes regular feedback. During their studies, candidates receive supervision and mentoring from qualified and experienced supervisors who provide guidance throughout the duration of their program.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g.,,Other qualifications equivalent to a Master’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

