  ('Master in Pharmacy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4356, '2 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master in Pharmacy is a postgraduate degree program designed for advanced students who wish to deepen their knowledge and expertise in pharmacy, preparing them for more demanding roles in areas such as community pharmacy, clinical pharmacy, veterinary pharmacy, military pharmacy, specialty pharmacy, and pharmacy informatics.

Candidates pursuing a Master in Pharmacy often go on to have successful careers in pharmacology, science writing, toxicology, and health regulation within medical institutions.

Throughout the program, students will engage in intensive research covering topics such as advanced pharmacy practice and pharmacotherapy, foundations of clinical science, pharmaceutical science concepts, pharmacology, drug disposition, applied pharmacotherapy, medical chemistry for pharmacy, medicinal product formulation, professional service, pharmacy placements, clinical and evidence-based practice, integrated therapeutics, and the leadership and management of health services, as well as nutrition, health, and biotechnology.

MAHSA University’s Master in Pharmacy program will equip advanced and discerning students with the skills and knowledge that will help them stand out in any competitive environment.

