  ('Master of Medical Science in Aesthetic Medicine', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 11374, '1.5 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'This program is designed for medical doctors seeking to deepen their knowledge of the science behind aesthetic medicine, including the legislation and application of evidence-based medicine (EBM) in their practice to ensure the delivery of safe and effective services. The program is taught by qualified and experienced academic staff, along with LCP-certified aesthetic practitioners, using state-of-the-art facilities and equipment to enhance the learning experience and support the intellectual and professional development of students. Additionally, students will have opportunities for research and may contribute to scientific publications in the field of aesthetic medicine.

The course spans three semesters, covering 10 modules with a total of 40 credits over 1.5 years. Assessments consist of 20-40% coursework and 50-60% final examinations and research projects, depending on the specific module.

