  ('Master of Medical Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4356, '2 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'MAHSA University’s Master of Medical Science (Anatomy) is primarily designed for students aiming to pursue doctoral studies (Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent).

This specialization provides training in research techniques and the preparation of scholarly papers, culminating in the development and defense of a thesis based on original research. The program introduces students to intensive study and research methods in selected areas of anatomy.

The curriculum includes a comprehensive oral examination covering the core anatomy courses, as well as a written scholarly project that addresses a contemporary issue within one of the various sub-disciplines of anatomy.

Additionally, the program offers opportunities to learn fundamental laboratory techniques used in anatomical research and allows students to assist in teaching graduate or undergraduate courses within the department.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["medical professional positions \nacademic research \nanatomy-related consulting"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Bachelor’s Degree in Zoology/ Life Sciences/ Biomedical/Health Sciences by a recognized university with CGPA of 3.00 or above.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Medical Sciences', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 6600, '1.5 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'MAHSA University’s Master of Medical Sciences is primarily designed for students who intend to pursue doctoral studies (Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent). Graduates will be equipped to apply their knowledge to real-life situations, develop social skills, and enhance critical thinking, with a focus on an integrative and technological understanding of biological systems at all levels. This program prepares them for careers in research and teaching within the fields of Medical and Health Sciences.

Graduates will gain competencies in idea management, communication, and leadership, enabling them to evaluate complex issues, plan effectively, implement solutions, and publish their findings. The program introduces students to intensive study and research methods in selected areas of medical sciences.

The curriculum is designed to align with current trends and needs, offering a highly sought-after blend of theoretical learning, e-learning, and practical sessions in laboratories and hospitals. It is accredited by the Malaysian Qualifications Agency and the Ministry of Higher Education.

The course is delivered by experienced lecturers across all fields, with the Faculty of Medicine & Biomedical Sciences boasting 116 qualified and experienced staff members in medical sciences.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Forensic laboratories\n\n\nFood production companies\n\n\nMedical and Health Services\n\n\nHealth Education\n\n\nHealth Communication\n\n\nPharmaceutical Companies\n\nHospitals\n\n\nUniversities\n\n\nForensic Laboratories\n\n\nFood Production Companies\n\n\nResearch Institutes"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor’s Degree (Level 6 MQF) in Biomedical Sciences, Life Sciences Health or equivalent qualifications from any institution of higher education accredited by the Faculty Postgraduate Academic Board and Senate with a minimum CGPA of 2.75

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Nursing', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4356, '2 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Nursing program is intellectually stimulating and designed to prepare students as nurse practitioners in their specialties, with a strong emphasis on evidence-based research. This program lays the groundwork for various leadership roles for professional nurses committed to delivering high-quality clinical services. Graduates will be responsible, accountable, and empowered to shape the future of the healthcare system, enhancing their professional expertise and enabling them to attain higher positions in advanced nursing.

As a student, you will explore essential aspects of the healthcare system and learn to consider the nursing profession within both local and global contexts. You will study nursing policies and politics, workforce and professional practice issues, healthcare financing and economics, as well as concepts of illness and health, including individual, family, and community expectations for healthcare quality and safety. The program prepares students to demonstrate critical thinking and problem-solving skills for effective decision-making, while also adapting to the changing health needs of the population. You will engage in discussions, debates, seminars, and presentations on relevant issues within a dynamic learning environment.

Graduates of this program will be equipped to support and guide team members creatively and innovatively, utilizing interdisciplinary approaches to deliver comprehensive, evidence-based healthcare practices.

The Master of Nursing program also serves as a foundation for doctoral studies in areas related to nursing interests.

The degree of Master of Nursing is awarded to students who satisfactorily complete the program and meet all other prescribed requirements.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Nurse unit manager\nNurse practitioner\nNurse educator"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'Bachelor degree in Nursing or nursing related.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Orofacial Sciences', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 24596, '1 year', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Orofacial Sciences program serves as a bridge between the Doctor of Dental Surgery and the three-year Doctorate program. This one-year program is a prerequisite for entering the Doctorate program. Completing both the one-year Master’s and the three-year Doctorate is necessary for graduates to be registered as dental specialists in their chosen field under the Malaysian Dental Act 2018.

This Master''s program offers local private practitioners and prospective dental lecturers the opportunity to enhance their skills in areas of personal interest. The curriculum includes four core modules: Applied Medical and Dental Sciences, Research Methodology, Research Project, and Community Dental Practice. The fifth module allows candidates to specialize in one of the following disciplines: Restorative Dentistry, Periodontology, or Orthodontics.

The research project will involve a minor study focused on the collection of clinical data for clinical audit outcomes, preliminary field studies, or introductory laboratory investigations. Research outputs may take the form of mini-dissertations or scientific reports.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Manage restorative cases with higher proﬁciency\n\n\nPursue higher education in Doctorate of Restorative Dentistry"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Bachelor of Dental Surgery Degree from a local University or its equivalent.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Physiotherapy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 10494, '1 year', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'MAHSA University offers a full-time Master of Physiotherapy program (1 year) and a part-time option (2 years), allowing candidates to specialize in either Musculoskeletal or Neurology. This innovative program is designed for physiotherapists looking to advance their careers while serving the community as evidence-based practitioners, equipped with strong clinical reasoning skills to make informed decisions regarding complex musculoskeletal and neurological issues.

To transition from an entry-level therapist to a specialist, candidates must complete a postgraduate degree with coursework in their chosen discipline. The credentials earned through this program can significantly enhance career progression as a Physiotherapist, opening doors to further research and various career advancement opportunities as specialists, educators, policymakers, or clinical managers.

The program employs a diverse range of teaching methods, including higher-order problem-solving activities, case studies, practice-based learning, peer support, and blended learning through e-Learning platforms. It comprises both coursework and research components, with a strong emphasis on developing advanced skills in the respective fields. The full-time program is primarily conducted on campus, with clinical placements at affiliated hospitals. The part-time program is delivered in blocks, featuring face-to-face sessions on campus supported by e-Learning. All modules are taught by practicing experts, specialists, and academics, ensuring alignment with the latest developments in the field.

A Bachelor’s Degree (Level 6 MQF) or equivalent with minimum CGPA of 2.50 in related field, as accepted by the HEP Senate.

