Spanning two semesters, the course covers four modules and includes a clinical attachment, totaling 20 credits within one year This program also creates a career pathway for medical doctors aiming to develop advanced knowledge, practical skills, and a professional attitude necessary for applying for the Letter of Credentialing and Privileging (LCP) Chapter 1 examination by the Ministry of Health Malaysia

Assessments consist of 20-40% coursework and 50-60% final examinations and clinical attachments, varying by module, ensuring a comprehensive evaluation of students'' competencies in the field.

