  ('Postgraduate Diploma in Management', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MAHSA University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Diploma', 4158, '0.9 years', '["Apr","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The business and management landscape is evolving at an unprecedented rate. In this era of rapid change and innovation, professionals and aspiring leaders must acquire the knowledge, skills, and adaptability needed to tackle complex challenges. The 9-month Post Graduate Diploma in Management (PGDM) is a dynamic and intensive program designed to equip students with the essential tools and insights for success in the business world.

The PGDM is a compact and focused postgraduate program that addresses key areas of management and business administration. It is tailored for individuals seeking a fast-track route to gain specialized knowledge and skills to boost their career prospects. Typically offered by business schools and management institutes, this program provides a comprehensive yet in-depth understanding of management principles.

The curriculum of the PGDM is thoughtfully designed to cover core business and management topics, ensuring students receive a well-rounded education in a relatively short timeframe. Common subjects include marketing, finance, operations, organizational behavior, strategic management, and entrepreneurship. The program’s condensed format often incorporates hands-on projects, case studies, and experiential learning opportunities.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

